@startuml K8sAIOps-Event-Flow
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title K8sAIOps Monitoring - Real-Time Event Flow

participant "Kubernetes\nCluster" as K8s
participant "KubernetesWatcher" as Watcher
participant "EventProcessor" as Processor
participant "Team Resolver\n(NamespaceTeamCache)" as TeamResolver
participant "Severity\nClassifier" as Classifier
participant "Dedup Cache" as Cache
participant "NotificationDispatcher" as Dispatcher
participant "SubscriptionRegistry" as Registry
participant "WebSocket\nServer" as WSServer
participant "Dashboard A\n(platform-ops)" as DashA
participant "Dashboard B\n(backend team)" as DashB

== 1. Kubernetes Event Occurs ==
K8s -> K8s: Pod CrashLoopBackOff\nin namespace: production\nwith label: team=backend

== 2. Event Detection ==
K8s -[#blue]> Watcher: Watch stream event:\ntype=Warning, reason=CrashLoopBackOff
note right of Watcher
    Watcher detects:
    namespace="production"
    resource="pod-xyz"
    kind="Pod"
    reason="CrashLoopBackOff"
end note

== 3. Event Processing ==
Watcher -[#green]> Processor: from_k8s_event(raw_object)

== 4. Team Resolution ==
Processor -[#orange]> TeamResolver: teams_for("production")
TeamResolver --> Processor: ["backend", "platform-ops"]\n(from namespace labels)
note right of TeamResolver
    Resolution chain:
    1. Check resource labels → "team=backend"
    2. Check namespace labels → "team=platform-ops"
    3. Combine & deduplicate
    Result: [backend, platform-ops]
end note

== 5. Severity Classification ==
Processor -[#red]> Classifier: classify("Warning", "CrashLoopBackOff")
Classifier --> Processor: Severity.CRITICAL
note right of Classifier
    CrashLoopBackOff matches
    _CRITICAL_REASON_EXACT
    → CRITICAL severity
end note

== 6. Deduplication ==
Processor -[#purple]> Cache: is_duplicate(fingerprint)?
note right of Cache
    fingerprint = sha256(
        "production/pod-xyz/CrashLoopBackOff"
    )[:16]

    Not in cache → New event
end note
Cache --> Processor: false (not duplicate)

== 7. Enriched Event Created ==
Processor -[#blue]> Processor: EnrichedEvent(\n  severity=CRITICAL,\n  namespace="production",\n  resource_name="pod-xyz",\n  reason="CrashLoopBackOff",\n  teams=["backend", "platform-ops"],\n  timestamp="2024-01-15T10:30:45Z"\n)

== 8. Dispatch to Subscribers ==
Processor -[#green]> Dispatcher: dispatch(enriched_event)
Dispatcher -[#green]> Registry: get_subscribers(event)

== 9. Subscription Filtering ==
note over Registry
    For each WebSocket subscriber:

    Dashboard A (alice@example.com):
    ✓ severity=CRITICAL in {WARNING, CRITICAL}
    ✓ namespace=production in {} (all namespaces)
    ✓ teams: {backend} ∩ {backend, platform-ops} ≠ ∅
    ✓ MATCH!

    Dashboard B (bob@example.com):
    ✓ severity=CRITICAL in {INFO, WARNING, CRITICAL}
    ✓ namespace=production in {production} ✓
    ✗ teams: {backend-dev} ∩ {backend, platform-ops} = ∅
    ✗ NO MATCH
end note

Registry --> Dispatcher: [ws_A]

== 10. Event Delivery ==
Dispatcher -[#red]> EventHistory: append(event_dict)
note right of EventHistory
    Store in in-memory deque
    (keeps last 500 events)
end note

Dispatcher -[#red]> WSServer: send(ws_A, json_payload)
WSServer -[#red]> DashA: {\n  "event_id": "evt-abc123-1705323045",\n  "severity": "CRITICAL",\n  "namespace": "production",\n  "resource_name": "pod-xyz",\n  "resource_kind": "Pod",\n  "reason": "CrashLoopBackOff",\n  "message": "Back-off restarting failed container",\n  "teams": ["backend", "platform-ops"],\n  "timestamp": "2024-01-15T10:30:45Z"\n}

note right of DashA
    Dashboard A receives
    & displays alert:

    🔴 [CRITICAL]
    CrashLoopBackOff
    production/pod-xyz
    Back-off restarting...
end note

DashB -[#gray]> DashB: (no notification - not subscribed to backend team)

== Alternative: Pod Lifecycle Watch ==
K8s -[#blue]> Watcher: Pod MODIFIED event\nstatus.phase=CrashLoopBackOff
Watcher -[#blue]> Processor: from_pod_object(pod, "MODIFIED")
note right of Processor
    Synthesize event from pod state
    instead of Kubernetes Event
    (useful for direct pod monitoring)
end note

== Periodic Namespace Cache Refresh ==
par Every NS_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS (default: 120s)
    TeamResolver -[#teal]> K8s: list_namespaces()
    K8s --> TeamResolver: [namespace_objects]
    note right of TeamResolver
        Update cached mapping:
        production → [backend, platform-ops]
        staging → [backend]
        dev → [ops-team] (fallback)
    end note
end

@enduml
